# Cloudflare Pages rewrite rules. Order matters; first match wins.
#
# The root serves the app's own root route (src/app/page.tsx, which renders
# Home) rather than redirecting to it. Status 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect:
# the browser stays on jornaevents.com and gets that file's HTML.
#
# It has to be /app/index.html and not /app/home/index.html. The client router
# resolves the path it was loaded at, and with basePath "/app" a pathname of "/"
# resolves to the app's "/" route — so serving any other page's HTML here would
# hydrate into a different page than the one that arrived.
#
# The target is /app/ and not /app/index.html. Pages normalises a served path by
# stripping "/index" and ".html", so naming the file directly makes the rule
# rewrite to something that matches itself — wrangler rejects it outright
# ("Infinite loop detected"), which with no static index.html left behind would
# mean the root 404s.
#
# The app itself is unchanged and still lives under /app; links from the root
# lead there. Deep links, emailed check-in and RSVP links, Stripe return URLs
# and the Supabase auth callback all keep working untouched.
/    /app/    200
